I have deactivated the Cache Assets switch in Nginx Proxy Manager.

With Nginx it should be the following configuration, as far as I understand it.
```
proxy_no_cache 1;
proxy_cache_bypass 1;
proxy_cache off;
```
https://github.com/NginxProxyManager/nginx-proxy-manager/issues/389#issuecomment-895485154

Hope I could help : )

Having exactly the same problem. Even after adding

proxy_no_cache 1;
proxy_cache_bypass 1;
proxy_cache off;

to NPM, the error still occurs from time to time. Then, the only way to login again is to delete all auth-tokens hand by hand:

occ user:auth-tokens:delete username token_number

Afterwards, you can login again. But after a while the error comes back.
